hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19154","Qutayba ibn Said narrated to us, and Qutayba wrote it to me: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Yahya ibn Maymun al-Hadrami, that Abu Musa al-Ghafiqi heard Uqba ibn Amir al-Juhani narrate upon the pulpit from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hadiths. So Abu Musa said: This companion of yours is either retentive or ruined. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) last covenanted to us that he said: Upon you is the Book of Allah, and you shall return to a people who love narration from me. So whoever says upon me what I did not say, let him take his seat of the Fire. And whoever retains from me anything, let him narrate it."
